  <h2 id="money">Money and the college filter</h2>

  <p>
    Use a conservative planning heuristic. Try to keep the college itself near 10 percent of your family's total education budget, and treat anything above about 20 percent as a serious caution that needs course-specific proof. This is a planning heuristic, not a law. The rest pays for living costs, tools, courses and the upskilling that raises income.
  </p>

  <p>
    Here is what that means next to the middle drop-year cost of about Rs 4.6 lakh. The budgets are illustrations, so replace them with your own.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
